IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-companies-domain`

§ `Part 7 — Arrangements, Reconstructions and Amalgamations`

-- ===========================================================================
-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), Part 7, ss 210–216A.
-- Source: SSO current version as at 07 Sep 2026.
--
-- ss 211A–211J: Repealed by Act 40 of 2018 (moved to IRDA).
-- ss 213–214: Repealed by S 675/2001.
--
-- This encoding covers the computable rules in ss 210–216A:
--   s 210: compromise/arrangement approval thresholds
--   s 211: information disclosure deadlines
--   s 212: reconstruction/amalgamation lodgement
--   s 215: compulsory acquisition (squeeze-out / sell-out)
--   s 215C–D: amalgamation proposal notice periods
--   s 215I–J: solvency statement penalties
--   s 216: oppression remedies lodgement
--   s 216A: derivative action notice period
-- ===========================================================================


§§ `Compromise and arrangement — s 210`


§§§ `s 210 — Approval thresholds`

-- s 210(3): adjournment requires majority in number representing 3/4 in value
-- s 210(3AB): binding compromise requires same dual threshold + court approval
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 210(3),(3AB)"
`compromise approval majority in number pct` MEANS 50
`compromise approval value threshold pct` MEANS 75

GIVEN `votes in favour`    IS A NUMBER
    , `votes present`      IS A NUMBER
    , `value in favour`    IS A NUMBER
    , `value present`      IS A NUMBER
    , `court approved`     IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `compromise or arrangement binding` IF
        `votes in favour` GREATER THAN (`votes present` DIVIDED BY 2)
    AND `value in favour` AT LEAST (`value present` TIMES 0.75)
    AND `court approved`

-- s 210(8)(b): reports available >= 7 days before meeting
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 210(8)(b)"
`compromise report availability days before meeting` MEANS 7

-- s 210(9): penalty for non-compliance with s 210(6) or (8)
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 210(9)"
`penalty for compromise information default` MEANS 2000

-- s 210(10A): trust money transfer to Official Receiver
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 210(10A)"
`trust money transfer earliest years` MEANS 2
`trust money transfer latest years` MEANS 10

GIVEN `years since money received` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may transfer compromise trust money to Official Receiver` IF
    `years since money received` AT LEAST 2

GIVEN `years since money received` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `must transfer compromise trust money to Official Receiver` IF
    `years since money received` AT LEAST 10


§§ `Information as to compromise — s 211`


§§§ `s 211 — Disclosure deadlines and penalties`

-- s 211(4): director/trustee must respond within 7 days of request
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 211(4)"
`compromise information response days` MEANS 7

-- s 211(5): penalty for non-compliance
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 211(5)"
`penalty for compromise disclosure default` MEANS 5000
`imprisonment for compromise disclosure default months` MEANS 12


§§ `Reconstruction and amalgamation — s 212`


§§§ `s 212 — Lodgement of court order`

-- s 212(3): lodge copy of order within 7 days
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 212(3)"
`reconstruction order lodgement days` MEANS 7

-- s 212(3): penalty for non-compliance
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 212(3)"
`penalty for reconstruction lodgement default` MEANS 2000


§§ `Compulsory acquisition — s 215`


§§§ `s 215 — Squeeze-out thresholds and deadlines`

-- s 215(1): scheme must be approved by >= 90% of shares (excl. treasury + transferee's)
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 215(1)"
`squeeze out approval threshold pct` MEANS 90

-- s 215(1): offer must be approved within 4 months
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 215(1)"
`squeeze out offer approval months` MEANS 4

-- s 215(1): transferee may give notice within 2 months of approval
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 215(1)"
`squeeze out notice months after approval` MEANS 2

-- s 215(1): dissenting shareholder court application deadline
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 215(1)"
`dissenting shareholder court application months` MEANS 1

-- s 215(1): alternative deadline after statement supplied
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 215(1)"
`dissenting shareholder court application days after statement` MEANS 14

-- s 215(1): the full squeeze-out test
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 215(1)"
GIVEN `shares approving`         IS A NUMBER
    , `total shares`             IS A NUMBER
    , `treasury shares`          IS A NUMBER
    , `transferee existing shares` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `squeeze out threshold met` IF
    `shares approving` AT LEAST
        ((`total shares` MINUS `treasury shares` MINUS `transferee existing shares`)
            TIMES 0.9)

-- s 215(1A): dissenting shareholder election deadline
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 215(1A)"
`dissenting shareholder election months` MEANS 1

-- s 215(2): dissenting shareholder may demand names/addresses within 1 month
-- Transferee not bound to acquire until 14 days after posting
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 215(2)"
`dissenting shareholder demand months` MEANS 1
`acquisition delay after statement days` MEANS 14

-- s 215(3): reverse squeeze-out (sell-out) — transferee holds >= 90% after transfer
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 215(3)"
GIVEN `shares held after transfer`  IS A NUMBER
    , `total shares in company`    IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reverse squeeze out threshold met` IF
    `shares held after transfer` AT LEAST
        (`total shares in company` TIMES 0.9)

-- s 215(3)(a): transferee must notify within 1 month of transfer
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 215(3)(a)"
`reverse squeeze out notification months` MEANS 1

-- s 215(3)(b): remaining holder may require acquisition within 3 months
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 215(3)(b)"
`sell out acquisition request months` MEANS 3

-- s 215(6): trust money to Official Receiver — same 2/10 year window
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 215(6)"
`acquisition trust money transfer earliest years` MEANS 2
`acquisition trust money transfer latest years` MEANS 10

-- s 215(12): control of body corporate for associate attribution
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 215(12)"
GIVEN `voting power pct in body corporate` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `controls body corporate for squeeze out` IF
    `voting power pct in body corporate` AT LEAST 50


§§ `Amalgamations — ss 215A–215K`


§§§ `s 215C — Amalgamation proposal notice periods`

-- s 215C(4),(5): send amalgamation materials >= 21 days before GM
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 215C(4)–(5)"
`amalgamation proposal notice days` MEANS 21


§§§ `s 215D — Short form amalgamation`

-- s 215D(3): notice to secured creditors >= 21 days before GM
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 215D(3)"
`short form amalgamation creditor notice days` MEANS 21


§§§ `s 215E — Creditor prejudice declaration`

-- s 215E(1)(e): directors must declare no creditor prejudiced if claims/assets
-- ratio is worse for amalgamated company than any amalgamating company
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 215E(1)(e)"
GIVEN `amalgamated claims`        IS A NUMBER
    , `amalgamated assets`        IS A NUMBER
    , `amalgamating claims`       IS A NUMBER
    , `amalgamating assets`       IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `creditor prejudice declaration required` IF
    (`amalgamated claims` DIVIDED BY `amalgamated assets`)
        GREATER THAN (`amalgamating claims` DIVIDED BY `amalgamating assets`)


§§§ `s 215I — Solvency statement penalties (amalgamating company)`

-- s 215I(6): false solvency statement penalty
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 215I(6)"
`penalty for false amalgamating solvency statement` MEANS 100000
`imprisonment for false amalgamating solvency statement years` MEANS 3


§§§ `s 215J — Solvency statement penalties (amalgamated company)`

-- s 215J(5): false solvency statement penalty
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 215J(5)"
`penalty for false amalgamated solvency statement` MEANS 100000
`imprisonment for false amalgamated solvency statement years` MEANS 3


§§§ `s 215K — Trust money transfer (amalgamation)`

-- s 215K(1): same 2/10 year window as s 210(10A) and s 215(6)
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 215K(1)"
`amalgamation trust money transfer earliest years` MEANS 2
`amalgamation trust money transfer latest years` MEANS 10


§§ `Oppression and derivative actions — ss 216–216A`


§§§ `s 216 — Oppression remedy lodgement`

-- s 216(5): lodge copy of order within 14 days
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 216(5)"
`oppression order lodgement days` MEANS 14

-- s 216(6): penalty for non-compliance
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 216(6)"
`penalty for oppression lodgement default` MEANS 1000


§§§ `s 216A — Derivative action notice`

-- s 216A(3)(a): complainant must give 14 days' notice to directors
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 216A(3)(a)"
`derivative action notice days` MEANS 14


-- ===========================================================================
-- TEST CASES
-- ===========================================================================

§§ `Part 7 — Illustrations`

-- s 210: compromise or arrangement binding
-- Majority in number (> 50%) AND 3/4 in value (>= 75%) AND court approved
#ASSERT `compromise or arrangement binding` 60 100 80 100 TRUE
#ASSERT `compromise or arrangement binding` 51 100 75 100 TRUE
-- Fails: not majority in number
#ASSERT NOT (`compromise or arrangement binding` 50 100 80 100 TRUE)
-- Fails: below 3/4 in value
#ASSERT NOT (`compromise or arrangement binding` 60 100 74 100 TRUE)
-- Fails: no court approval
#ASSERT NOT (`compromise or arrangement binding` 60 100 80 100 FALSE)

-- s 210(10A): trust money transfer timing
#ASSERT `may transfer compromise trust money to Official Receiver` 2
#ASSERT `may transfer compromise trust money to Official Receiver` 5
#ASSERT NOT (`may transfer compromise trust money to Official Receiver` 1)
#ASSERT `must transfer compromise trust money to Official Receiver` 10
#ASSERT NOT (`must transfer compromise trust money to Official Receiver` 9)

-- s 215(1): squeeze-out threshold
-- 900 approving out of (1000 total - 50 treasury - 50 transferee) = 900 eligible
-- 90% of 900 = 810 -> 900 >= 810 -> met
#ASSERT `squeeze out threshold met` 900 1000 50 50
-- 800 approving -> 800 < 810 -> not met
#ASSERT NOT (`squeeze out threshold met` 800 1000 50 50)
-- Edge case: exactly 90%
#ASSERT `squeeze out threshold met` 810 1000 50 50

-- s 215(3): reverse squeeze-out (sell-out) threshold
-- 900 of 1000 = 90% -> met
#ASSERT `reverse squeeze out threshold met` 900 1000
-- 899 of 1000 = 89.9% -> not met
#ASSERT NOT (`reverse squeeze out threshold met` 899 1000)

-- s 215(12): control of body corporate
#ASSERT `controls body corporate for squeeze out` 50
#ASSERT `controls body corporate for squeeze out` 75
#ASSERT NOT (`controls body corporate for squeeze out` 49)

-- s 215E(1)(e): creditor prejudice declaration required
-- Amalgamated: 600/1000 = 0.6; Amalgamating: 400/1000 = 0.4 -> worse -> required
#ASSERT `creditor prejudice declaration required` 600 1000 400 1000
-- Equal ratios -> not required
#ASSERT NOT (`creditor prejudice declaration required` 400 1000 400 1000)
-- Better ratio -> not required
#ASSERT NOT (`creditor prejudice declaration required` 300 1000 400 1000)
